    fix(ask): persist the JEV-proposed question so answer --question-id works. Addresses AUG-035.
    
    `ask` printed the question JEV picked and stored nothing, so the next move in the README's
    loop — `answer --question-id Q-...` — refused the engine's own suggestion, and `feedback`
    (thin decisions only) was the sole writer of question rows. `ask` now stores the proposal it
    prints: one `question` row (`status=open`, `qclass=ask_proposed`, `ring=1`, the text it
    printed, the gate's noul in `jev_already_answered` with `jev_checked_at`) plus one `facet`
    row per facet, printed as `stored question: <id>`.
    
    The store is fail-closed: a proposal below T_SUBJECT, one the gate scores answered, one with
    no verdict at all, and one whose text is already open all store nothing and say why; a
    refused insert stores nothing and keeps ask's exit code 0. Nothing else is invented — no
    `opens` edge (the proposal names no decision) and no `domain`. Docs stop claiming `ask` is
    not a write (VERBS.md; the diagnostics note is folded in by the dogfood commit).
    
    Six new cases assert the rows: the stored text/confidence/facets, the loop completing
    through `answer --question-id`, no duplicate on a second ask, and each refusal path leaving
    the `question` table empty. Full suite green: 119 passed (404s); tests/gate.sh PASS (pytest
    542s + the 21-assertion smoke loop).
    
    Live probe (scratch namespace, real JEV, torn down): 1 of 4 asks cleared T_SUBJECT (0.47 vs
    0.24/0.32/0.43) and the loop closed end to end — `stored question: Q-000001`, then
    `answer --question-id Q-000001` wrote the `closes` edge and the question went `answered` with
    its facets closed. The other three printed `question not stored: the proposal is below
    threshold 0.45`. That measured gate behavior in live use is AUG-041 (filed by the dogfood
    lane), and the stored text being JEV's criterion slug rather than a sentence is AUG-042.
